  + [requirement] is refine insertion bridge geometry and blocked-state feedback against the Chat/Cutting layout
  + [fork_commit] is bb416517
  + [solution] is the bridge rail now has an explicit component ref and the Cutting insertion markers expose data-insertion-index anchors
  + [solution] is the bridge arrow synchronizes to the active insertion marker as insertion position, visible panes, selected source, active cut count, or Cutting scroll state changes
  + [solution] is drag behavior remains user-controlled and temporarily suppresses auto-sync while the pointer is actively moving the arrow
  + [data_design_reason] is insertion_position is now represented as inspectable UI state linked to the cut ordering relation
  + [ui_interaction_reason] is the transform affordance visually tracks the destination location instead of floating at an arbitrary default y coordinate

  = must: preserve user drag as the way to choose insertion position
  = must: keep bridge hidden when Chat or Cutting is hidden
  = must: keep insertion markers as visible feedback for the current cut position

